        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>We take the safety, security and well-being of our users very seriously. As a growing in popularity website for playing board game other people, we take pride in connecting people every day. While there is always a change to meet people with bad intentions outside of BoardGameHive.ro website, we try to protect our members by offering them tips on how to behave and to what to expect from the others, because we firmly believe any incident of misconduct or criminal behavior is one too many. </p>
              <p>We are continuously exploring new updates, technologies and potential partnerships to enhance and inform our safety efforts while fostering a respectful environment for meeting new people to play board games with them. Information about our safety tools and practices can be found below. Whether you’re in Bucharest, Madrid, Paris or in any other town/country - our goal remains the same: a safe and positive experience for users on our platform.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>



        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Our Safety Tools</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>We utilize automated and manual moderation and review tools, systems and processes - and invest resources - to prevent, monitor and remove inappropriate behavior (impersonation, harassment and more) from our BoardGameHive.ro website.</p>
              <p>These tools include a reports of profiles for red-flag language and images; manual reviews of suspicious profiles, activity, and user generated reports; shadow-banning suspicious accounts; as well as blocking of email addresses, phone numbers, and other identifiers associated with bad actors.</p>
              <p>We have a zero-tolerance policy on harassment and encourage our community to report any instance of misconduct and/or anyone who violates our <a href="/legal/community_guidelines">Community Guidelines</a> or <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Use</a>, via the reporting tool featured on all BoardGameHive.ro invites or by contacting us online through <a href="/feedbackus">FeedbackUs</a>. In the event that we receive such a report, we will take the appropriate measures, which may include flagging the user with a “stain” which will be displayed in the user’s profile inside the reputation section and directly if you hover over the user’s avatar inside the invites (so that all the users can see what the reported user has done), removing the content, banning the user, or notifying the appropriate law enforcement resources.</p>
              <p>We are constantly evaluating and refining our processes, and will always work with law enforcement, where possible, to protect our users.</p>
              <p>Response to Reports of Assault: BoardGameHive.ro users can easily report instances of abuse or assault online. We strongly encourage any user who believes they have been a victim of a crime to report it to law enforcement. Our team works to promptly investigate reported crimes, assess and take appropriate action, and fully cooperates with law enforcement in any investigation.</p>
              <p>When a user reports an assault to BoardGameHive.ro, we attempt to identify the alleged perpetrator and block the associated account. </p>
              <p>User Education: We offer safety tips online, to educate and empower users to make smart and safe choices while interacting on BoardGameHive.ro.</p>

              <a href="/legal/cookie_policy">View our Tips for Staying Safe here</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>



        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Fraud</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>We take the issue of fraud very seriously at BoardGameHive.ro. We have a zero-tolerance policy on predatory behavior of any kind. Ultimately, no one, whether they met on BoardGameHive.ro or not, should ever send money to someone they haven't met in person. In addition, we encourage our members to report any individual who has requested financial information via our reporting tool inside <a href="/feedbackus">FeedbackUs</a>. Those two steps will greatly assist in stopping almost every scam in its tracks and help protect the next potential victim.  </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>



        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Data Privacy and Platform Security</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Our users’ privacy is a top priority at BoardGameHive.ro, and we work diligently to ensure that we go above and beyond applicable privacy laws and industry standards. We know that your time on the BoardGameHive.ro website is a private matter and have strict policies and technical systems in place, including encryption for user photos and messages and tools that restrict employee access to user communications and other user data. When it comes to BoardGameHive.ro users’ data, our sole mandate is keeping our users safe and their data private.</p>
              <p>Your data is yours. As such, users can request a copy of their data through <a href="/feedbackus">FeedbackUs</a> at any time. The most up-to-date information on our data practices is always available to the general public through our <a href="/legal/privacy_policy">Privacy Policy</a>, which can be also accessed through our BoardGameHive.ro website.</p>
              <p>Additionally, we are constantly improving our defenses in the battle against those with malicious intent.  However, we do not discuss any specific security tools we use or enhancements we may implement to best protect our users and avoid tipping off any would-be offenders.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>


        <br>

        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Additional Policies and Information</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Our fundamental goal is to introduce our community of users to the chance to play board games with other people. And while this is a lot of fun, it’s important to remember that there are <a href="/legal/community_guidelines">Community Guidelines</a> that our users must abide by to help make BoardGameHive.ro the best website for playing board games with other people.</p>
              <p>We encourage our users to report any instance of bad behavior on or off our platform. Reporting a user for inappropriate conduct is straightforward and easy to do. On any given invite where you have participated with the user you wish to report, you can tap the user’s profile image, over the lion shaped icon, and select the category you wish to report. Users can also report another user by submitting a help request online at <a href="/feedbackus">FeedbackUs</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p>Below are more details about some of our policies that we have implemented to keep BoardGameHive.ro more safe.</p>


        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Dedication to Inclusion</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>No matter your gender identity, sexual orientation, ethnicity, or background, BoardGameHive.ro welcomes you. We strive to make BoardGameHive.ro the most inclusive platform for meeting new people and have worked to constantly improve our practices.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>


        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Harassment</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>We have a zero-tolerance policy for harassment on our platform. We encourage all users to report any unacceptable behavior so that the community team can investigate and take appropriate action.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>


        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Underage Usage</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>BoardGameHive.ro is for users 18+, and we work hard to vigilantly maintain an adults only community. We utilize a network of automated and manual moderation and review tools, systems and processes - and invest significant resources - to prevent and remove minors from our website.</p>
              <p>These tools may include automatic scans of profiles for red-flag language and images, manual reviews of suspicious profiles, activity, and user generated reports, as well as blocking email addresses, phone numbers and other identifiers associated with underage users trying to circumvent these restrictions. We also depend on our users to report any profiles that may depict a minor, so that we can investigate and remove, accordingly.</p>
              <p>We do not want minors on BoardGameHive.ro. Period.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>


        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Solicitation/Prostitution</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Solicitation of any kind - whether attempting to buy or sell - is against our <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Use</a>. If a user encounters a profile violating our terms, we encourage them to report via the self-reporting tool featured on all BoardGameHive.ro profiles or online.  Making such a report allows our dedicated community team to take appropriate measures, which may include removing the profile or banning the user.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>


        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Illegal Substances</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Profiles (or BoardGameHive.ro users) promoting illegal substances violate our <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Use</a> and we will to remove these profiles from the website, whenever we become aware of them. If a user encounters a profile violating our terms, we encourage them to report it in within the website.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>


        <b>
          <p>If you feel you are in immediate danger or need emergency assistance, call your local law enforcement agency. Here are some options available: </p>
          <ul>
            <li> •	Call 112 – for Romania, </li>
            <li> •	112 is also the European emergency phone number, available everywhere in the EU, free of charge. 112 network-based location.</li>
            <li> •	Call 911 – for U.S. or Canada</li>
          </ul>
        </b>






        

